cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use flybots in teaching, research or software, please cite it as
  below. Each algorithm also cites its own source in its module docstring;
  please cite those too when your work relies on a specific method.
type: software
title: "flybots: flight algorithms for autonomous UAVs, from scratch"
abstract: >-
  flybots is an open-source Python framework of autonomous-UAV algorithms
  written from scratch: multirotor, fixed-wing and VTOL flight models with
  the physics written out in full, control, planning, estimation,
  perception, swarming and safety algorithms, a runnable simulation for
  each, and reinforcement-learning environments. It is built to be extended:
  an algorithm is implemented once, next to its citation, and comes with a
  simulation, tests that assert on flight behaviour, and a documentation
  page, so complex methods can be read, run, modified and explained.
authors:
  - family-names: Lejeune
    given-names: Erwin
version: 2.0.0 # x-release-please-version
date-released: 2026-08-27 # x-release-please-date
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/guilyx/flybots"
url: "https://guilyx.github.io/flybots/"
keywords:
  - uav
  - drone
  - quadrotor
  - fixed-wing
  - vtol
  - robotics
  - control
  - path planning
  - state estimation
  - reinforcement learning
  - education
